{
  "$description": "Frame design preview tokens (stage 1). Decided by the Design System Lead (2026-11-19): sizes mobile / tablet / desktop (size.viewport-*); name above the frame in label + text.primary, size in body-sm + text.secondary; frame on background.page, 1px border.subtle, radius.8, shadow.frame; device bar (status bar on mobile and tablet, browser bar on desktop); hover = border.strong; selected = 2px border.focus on the frame; keyboard focus = 2px border.focus outline offset by space.4; empty = icon + centered text in text.secondary. Then approved: label-gap and label-row-gap space.8; device bar on background.page with a border.subtle line, label-sm + text.primary, icon-size.16, padding space.16 / space.8, desktop address field background.subtle + radius.16; empty = add_box icon-size.32 + 'Drop components here' in body, gap space.8; 'canvas' = background.subtle (context background only, the Canvas B142 decides its own). Props: size (mobile default / tablet / desktop), selected, empty; long name cut with an ellipsis at the frame width; the content scrolls inside the frame. The frame is scaled down in the preview; its real size is the size.viewport-* token. 'selected' and 'empty' are shown on the mobile size. Accessibility decisions (2026-11-19): hover and focus also use the state layers (state-layer.hover / .focus, in text.primary, over the whole frame); focus and selected show together (selected outline on the frame + focus outline offset by space.4 around it); status bar icon gap space.4, device bar item gap space.8, empty message padding space.16.",
  "text": "Home",
  "previewStates": [
    "default",
    "hover",
    "focus"
  ],
  "previewMinWidth": "360px",
